nationally. The company operates in two segments: MacDermid Alpha Electronics Solutions and Element Specialties. Its MacDermid Alpha Electronics Solutions segment provides assembly solutions, including surface mount technologies, pastes fluxes, thermal management materials, coatings, and other attachment materials; circuitry solutions, such as circuit board metallization, circuit formation products, electronic materials, surface finishes, and film and smart surface solutions; and semiconductor solutions, which includes semiconductor assembly and wafer level packaging materials. This segment serves the mobile communications, computers, automobiles, and aerospace equipment industries. The Element Specialties segment offers industrial solutions, including electroless nickel, plating products, pre-treatment and cleaning solutions, functional conversion coatings, and water treatment; and energy solutions, which includes offshore fluids. This segment serves the aerospace, automotive, construction, consumer electronics, and oil and gas production end markets. The company was formerly known as Platform Specialty Products Corporation and changed its name to Element Solutions Inc in January 2019. Element Solutions Inc was founded in 1785 and is based in Miami Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Benjamin  Gliklich | CEO & Director | Age 40 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $491K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $44K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Element Solutions Inc. is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $8.0B market cap on $2.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 42%.","The business throws off $228M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 66% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6639284104519432},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $17.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-17851793.32},{"text":"Significant goodwill (44% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Gross margin tops the Basic Materials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Element Solutions (ESI) Upgraded to Strong Buy: Here's What You Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029734/element-solutions-esi-upgraded-to-strong-buy-here-s-what-you-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_12_zacks_rank_upgrade-3029734","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794585604.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"732,243 Element Solutions Inc. $ESI Shares Sold by New South Capital Management Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/732243-element-solutions-inc-esi-shares-sold-by-new-south-capital-management-inc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482836.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Element Solutions (ESI) Stock Outpacing Its Basic Materials Peers This Year?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028067/is-element-solutions-esi-stock-outpacing-its-basic-materials-peers-this-year?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_1-3028067","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794427631.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Element Solutions (ESI) Pulled Back, Is It Still 30% Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-esi/element-solutions/news/element-solutions-esi-pulled-back-is-it-still-30-