ty of 48% and a beta of 1.20, it amplifies market moves.","Liquidity is deep, with about $139.7M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 50% in the 2020 crash and 35% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $19.88 (margin of safety -66%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 24%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $10.92 to $34.45 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Basic Materials peers: P/E 38.9 vs 16.3, EV/EBITDA 16.9 vs 8.3 and P/FCF 35.3 vs 22.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 57% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 2.8% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.4% (vs the 8% bar).","The 12 covering analysts target $47.33 on average, 43% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 6% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.8%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.35).","It runs a 42% gross margin and converts 9% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.52x.","ROE of 7% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 2.6% of revenue on R&D and 2.3% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.0x net debt to EBITDA ($626.5M of cash against $1.6B of debt), above the 1.5x gate.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 3.68).","Goodwill makes up 44% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.0% over 3 years and 6.6% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 100%).","At current returns, reinvesting 70% of profits supports about 4.5% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -1.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are contracting (-1.2% trend).","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (2.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 13, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 6.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 98%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (6 sales, net $17.9M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.3% (0.3% in buybacks and 1.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 5,200 employees, each generates about $491K of revenue, 0.8x the Basic Materials median, and revenue has grown 10.6% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $44K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.8M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $11K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":30,"head":"Watch: priced 66% above its $19.88 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $10.92\u2013$34.45 range.","pros":["12 analysts' mean target $47.33 (+43%)","12-1 month momentum +40%"],"cons":["Trades 66% above fair value of $19.88","ROIC 6.4% vs WACC 9.8%","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 38.9x vs sector 16.3x","EV/EBITDA 16.9x vs sector 8.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["its composite (32) is below 39","no margin of safety","the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","it earns less than its cost of capital","too few checks pass (conviction 30)"],"buy_below":16.9,"vc":{"base":19.88,"base_src":"dcf","bear":10.92,"bull":34.45,"alt_median":6.03,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.2949,"dispersion":0.2408,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","DCF is 229% above the other models' median ($6.03)","bull case is 3.2x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":16.2619,"ev_ebitda":8.35,"pfcf":22.4216,"pb":2.0723,"r